# ledger/languages — the extensions of the languages that BUILD THE SYSTEM in this repo.
# A staged file matching one of these fires ledger/check.sh at commit. ledger/check.sh
# must check every language listed here, or that language can weaken unseen (a fail-open).
#
# Only needed when the gate's root-marker auto-detection is wrong for you: the system is
# built from more than one language, a build marker is nested (not at the repo root), or
# the tree contains vendored/tooling sources in a language the system is NOT built in.
# One extension per line; leading dot optional; `#` starts a comment.
#
# Example — a Scala backend plus a nested TypeScript frontend:
.scala
.sc
.sbt
.ts
.tsx
